  "requisiteAndIncompatibility": {
    "status": "present",
    "officialText": "Students with excellent results in either the ACT Specialist Mathematics double major, NSW HSC Mathematics Extension 2 or equivalent may take this course together with MATH1115 in the first year. For many students taking MATH1115 in their first year, MATH1005 would be a more appropriate companion choice. If you are not sure which courses to take in your first year, please consult the MSI First-year Coordinator. All other students may enrol in this course if they have completed MATH1116 with a mark of at least 50, or MATH1113 with a mark of at least 60, or MATH1005 with a mark of at least 70, or MATH1013 or MATH1014 with a mark of at least 80. Incompatible: MATH2322, MATH3104, MATH2320, MATH3116 or MATH6222.",
